course: dictionary
lesson: 15078
title: Rigorously: careful and exact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rigorously is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. When something is done rigorously, it is done very carefully and thoroughly, with every detail checked. «The scientists measured the plants rigorously, every day for a month.» The word rigorously tells you that they did not skip anything.
explain: Rigorously can also mean strictly, without making exceptions. «The school rules are rigorously enforced, so nobody is allowed to be late.» Here, the rules are followed every time, for everyone. There are no special cases.
explain: Look at the words around rigorously to find its meaning. Words like checked, measured, every detail and every step are clues. They show that care and thoroughness matter. If you swap in careful and thorough and the sentence still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Rigorously is an adverb, so it tells you how an action is done.
fact: «Rigorously» means in a very careful, thorough and exact way.
fact: «Rigorously» can also mean strictly, without any exceptions.
fact: In a fair test, scientists must measure rigorously, using the same conditions and repeating their measurements.
fact: In maths, a proof is rigorous when every step follows from the one before.
exercise: «The scientists checked every measurement rigorously.» What does rigorously mean? | *Very carefully and thoroughly, checking every detail | Quickly, without bothering to look twice | Only sometimes | Loudly, so everyone could hear
exercise: «The library rules are rigorously followed.» What does rigorously suggest about the rules? | Followed sometimes, if people feel like it | *Followed strictly, with no exceptions | Forgotten by everyone | Followed in a hurry
exercise: Find the word closest in meaning to rigorously. | *thorough | careless | loud | slow
test: In a fair test, why must the scientists measure rigorously? | To hide the results from the teacher | To make the results careless, so they are quick to write down | *To make sure the results are exact and can be trusted | To make the plant grow faster
test: In maths, a proof is checked rigorously when | one step is skipped to save time | the answer is guessed | *every step is checked and follows from the one before | the answer is written in pencil
exam: Which sentence uses rigorously correctly? | She sang rigorously at the party | The rain fell rigorously all day | He tied his laces rigorously and never looked at them | *The team checked every answer rigorously before they sent it in
